The [component registry](https://github.com/joelhooks/rat-stack/blob/main/apps/mischief/scripts/component-registry.ts) defines agent and human renderers.
The [code-snippets design brief](/lore/code-snippets) gives both renderers one snippet model.

The proposed `CodeSnippet` carries:
- Selected source text and original line numbers.
- Highlighted lines and collapsed gaps.
- Repository, commit, path, and source link.
- Diagnostics.

HTML adds colour, a filename, numbered lines, and a source link.
Agent Markdown adds the repository, commit, path, and original line numbers, plus a Markdown code block.
Both renderers use the same source facts.

Both views preserve the same source facts.
The planned property compares each view with the pinned source.

[Whole-file tokenization](/lore/tokenize-before-slicing) supplies the tokens.
[Engine-neutral tokens](/lore/engine-neutral-tokens-keep-adapters-replaceable) keep renderer input independent of Shiki.

See [the glossary](/glossary) for snippet model and renderer parity, the term for views preserving the same source facts.
